  annotation "note_1771574989023_1", anchor: "These materials predate the era when orcas turned to raiding", text: "\"Turned to raiding.\" I wrote that. A carved devotional artifact depicting a dead god, produced during an era of contact rather than conflict, and I framed the transition as something the orcas did unilaterally. The deep-ice trade records from the Ledge passage show penguin settlements expanding into orca hunting grounds across three successive generations. Something turned them. The passive voice is doing work I should not have asked of it.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
